+/**
+ * Leaves a due progress clean call through the dispatcher with a fixed owned
+ * obligation. budget must be an allocated raw-TLS slot of the calling thread,
+ * negative on entry, and retained until thread exit. quantum and charged must
+ * be positive and at most UINT_MAX. mc must contain DR_MC_ALL and explicit app PC.
+ *
+ * After complete cache-exit processing on a fresh dstack, the core adds quantum
+ * BEFORE each payment, repeating while budget is negative. It then refunds the
+ * captured old charged count exactly once, releases the record, and resolves
+ * the application PC again. This function never returns to the clean call.
+ *
+ * pay must be a stable client-library function executing only a finite marked
+ * progress syscall, returning its positive result, without locks, DR calls,
+ * cache references, or application effects. It is not an arbitrary blocking
+ * callback interface. Only this owned private interval is non-transferable;
+ * delayable application signals remain pending until payment/refund completes.
+ * Synchronous faults retain their ordinary DR fault handling. Recursive entry
+ * is invalid. The caller must not free the TLS allocation during the obligation.
+ */
+void
+dr_app_progress_exit(dr_mcontext_t *mc, ptr_int_t *budget, ptr_int_t quantum,
+                     ptr_int_t charged, ptr_int_t (*pay)(void));
